
Graph Representation using Adjacency List:

========================================================================================================

1. Introduction

An adjacency list stores a graph as a collection of lists. Every vertex keeps a list of the vertices that are directly connected to it.
It uses less memory than an adjacency matrix when the graph is sparse.

Sample graph used in this document:

- Vertices: A, B, C, D, E
- Edges (undirected): A-B, A-C, B-D, C-D, D-E

